# LEAN Alpaca AI Trading API

API bridge for connecting AI/LEAN systems with Alpaca.

## Default mode

The application uses Alpaca Paper Trading by default.

ALPACA_PAPER=true

## Railway Variables

Set these variables in Railway:

ALPACA_API_KEY=YOUR_ALPACA_PAPER_KEY
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=YOUR_ALPACA_PAPER_SECRET

ALPACA_PAPER=true

APP_API_KEY=CREATE_A_LONG_RANDOM_API_KEY

ENABLE_TRADING=false

MAX_ORDER_USD=100
MAX_POSITION_USD=500
MAX_POSITIONS=10

## Start

The Dockerfile starts:

uvicorn api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT

## API

GET /

GET /health

GET /api/status

GET /api/account

GET /api/positions

GET /api/orders

POST /api/order

DELETE /api/orders/{order_id}

DELETE /api/orders

DELETE /api/positions/{symbol}

DELETE /api/positions

GET /api/clock

GET /api/calendar

## Example order

POST /api/order

Headers:

X-API-Key: YOUR_APP_API_KEY

JSON:

{
    "symbol": "AAPL",
    "side": "buy",
    "notional": 50,
    "order_type": "market",
    "time_in_force": "day"
}

Trading must be enabled:

ENABLE_TRADING=true

Otherwise orders are rejected.

## Security

Never put Alpaca keys directly inside Python source code.

Never commit .env files.

Use Railway Variables.
